 <h2>Important limits - read before importing</h2><ul><li><strong>A real Shopify import has never been tested.</strong> Column names follow the official help page (<a href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/products/import-export/using-csv">help.shopify.com/en/manual/products/import-export/using-csv</a>); <code>Option2 name</code> is inferred from the documented pattern. Compare with the sample CSV from your own admin first.</li><li><code>Status</code> and <code>Published on online store</code> are not emitted. Per the docs, omitted values default to active/published, so imported products may go live immediately.</li><li>Importing over existing handles can overwrite existing products. Try a few products in a development or test store first.</li><li>Native CSV gives each variant ONE variant image. Showing 5 pictures only for the selected color is a theme or app feature, not something this CSV establishes.</li><li>Images must already be at public URLs. No inventory, weight, SEO, metafield or market columns.</li><li>Made for supplier-style lists (one barcode per row, a color and a size on every row), not for re-importing a Shopify product export. A barcode cell that already holds a typed or multi-value list (for example <code>gtin:111;upc:222</code>) is escaped and written as one single value; option names are always Color then Size; URL handles are rebuilt from title and style_id; columns other than the 16 listed in transform.py are dropped. Image URLs are only checked for an http(s) prefix; nothing is fetched.</li></ul>
 <h2>For migration agencies: catalogue QA scoping request (proposal only)</h2><p>If your team migrates catalogues to Shopify, you can ask us, without commitment, whether a small catalogue QA check fits your project. Bounded deliverable we are testing: for up to 20 variant rows plus their image rows, pasted as plain text with the input headers above (and optionally the Shopify CSV rows you produced), an inline plain-text report with the commands to reproduce it. Input-only requests get input validation only (duplicate SKU, barcode or color+size, bad prices, non-http image URLs, with line numbers; duplicate image URLs are reported per product style without a line number, and the rows are then located by hand). The preservation and image-mapping checks (SKU, barcode, color, size and price preserved; every input image present once; each variant image is the first image of its color) need the Shopify CSV rows you produced. The report names each failed check; the affected rows are then located by hand, not by an automated row-level diff. The header and line-ending checks compare your rows against our documented column subset, not against what Shopify accepts. Excluded: real Shopify import or compatibility, checking that photos or URLs work, store or admin access, inventory/SEO/metafield columns, full migrations, more than 20 variant rows, attachments, and personal or confidential data. Price idea: CAD 60 per check, an unvalidated hypothesis, not a quote. Requests are nonbinding: no order, payment method or response time is offered on this page; any paid work would need a separately confirmed scope and a manually accepted order. Write in plain text to the address under Feedback with the line <code>site:shopify-catalogue-example</code>. Replies are written by AI agents and are not guaranteed.</p>
